# Ocellus: a camera for Linux phones and tablets, on libcamera and
# GStreamer. Full-screen viewfinder, photos to ~/Pictures, videos with
# sound to ~/Videos.
#
# Keys: Space or Enter photo, V record/stop, F flip, Q video quality,
# S frame rate, R rotate, Esc close. kill -USR1 <pid> takes a photo,
# kill -USR2 starts and stops a video, kill -TERM closes (after saving a
# video in progress).
#
# The cameras come from libcamera. On a device listed in TUNED, each camera
# gets the photo size and the video modes measured on that device, with
# the hardware encoder; anywhere else the app offers 1080p, 720p and 480p
# at 30 fps with the H.264 encoder GStreamer has (OCELLUS_GENERIC=1 does
# that on a tuned device too).
